{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012wWq5NsmU6HwTcZb9fUHqC","type":"tool_result","content":"1190:      \"id\": \"US-052\",\n1191-      \"title\": \"LessonChat — sliding side panel UI scaffold + persisted draft in localStorage\",\n1192-      \"description\": \"As a learner, I want a sliding side panel inside lessons where I can compose questions to an AI tutor and have my draft preserved across page reloads, so I can come back to a question without retyping.\",\n1193-      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n1194-        \"Right column of lesson view (US-015 chatCol) becomes a controlled panel: 0px when closed, 320px when open; transition 180ms; prefers-reduced-motion disables animation\",\n1195-        \"Toggle: existing tutor button (⌘.) in lesson toolbar (currently disabled/grey from US-015) becomes active and toggles the panel; ⌘. keyboard shortcut (US-021) likewise toggles\",\n1196-        \"Panel chrome: header with 'AI Tutor' title + close X button; scrollable body for message list; sticky footer with composer (textarea + Send button + Stop button placeholder)\",\n1197-        \"Composer textarea autoresizes (max 6 lines); Enter inserts newline; ⌘+Enter (or Ctrl+Enter) triggers Send; Send button disabled when textarea empty or whitespace-only\",\n1198-        \"Message list area shows placeholder copy when empty: 'Ask anything about this lesson — I have its content as context.' centered, --text-tertiary --fs-sm\",\n1199-        \"Send (in this story) appends a user-message bubble to the message list and clears the textarea — no backend call yet (backend lands in US-053); a placeholder assistant bubble with 'Backend not connected — try again after US-053 ships' is appended for visibility during dev\",\n1200-        \"Draft persistence: textarea value mirrored to `localStorage['lessonChatDraft:<courseSlug>:<lessonSlug>']` on each keystroke (debounced 200ms); restored on mount\",\n1201-        \"Draft cleared from localStorage when message Send appends to message list (text now lives in chat history)\",\n1202-        \"Panel state (open/closed) persisted to `localStorage['lessonChat-open']` (boolean string)\",\n1203-        \"Verify in browser using playwright-skill: open lesson, click ⌘. button, confirm panel slides open; type a draft, reload page, confirm draft restored; send message, confirm appears in list and draft cleared from localStorage\",\n1204-        \"Typecheck passes\"\n1205-      ],\n1206-      \"priority\": 52,\n1207-      \"passes\": false,\n1208-      \"notes\": \"UI scaffold only — no Claude integration in this story. US-053 wires backend.\",\n1209-      \"tags\": [\n1210-        \"ui\"\n1211-      ]\n1212-    },\n1213-    {\n1214-      \"id\": \"US-053\",\n1215-      \"title\": \"LessonChat — backend integration (Claude Agent SDK with Max plan, fallback to claude -p subprocess)\",\n1216-      \"description\": \"As the LessonChat panel, I want a backend route that calls Claude either via the Claude Agent SDK (using the user's Claude Max plan) or by spawning the `claude -p` subprocess as a fallback, so users don't pay per-token.\",\n1217-      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n1218-        \"POST /api/lesson-chat accepts { courseSlug, lessonSlug, sectionId?, message, history?: Array<{role: 'user'|'assistant', content: string}> }; returns { assistant: string } as full block (no streaming yet — streaming lands in US-055)\",\n1219-        \"Server-side connector module src/lib/lessonChat/connector.ts with two implementations: (a) agentSdkConnector — uses @anthropic-ai/claude-agent-sdk authenticated via the local Claude Code subscription/session (no API key); (b) subprocessConnector — spawns `claude -p \\\"<prompt>\\\" --output-format json` via child_process.spawn, parses JSON output, extracts assistant text\",\n1220-        \"Connector selection at server boot: try Agent SDK first — verify it can authenticate against local Claude subscription without an explicit API key; if SDK unavailable, package missing, or auth fails, fall back to subprocess; selection cached per server process (not re-detected per request)\",\n--\n1224:        \"Wire LessonChat panel (US-052) Send button to POST this route; show a typing-indicator (animated dots) bubble while awaiting; render assistant bubble on response; on 503 render error bubble with the message\",\n1225-        \"Vitest tests cover: subprocess connector with mocked spawn returns parsed text; non-zero exit handled; timeout handled; selection logic falls back when SDK throws\",\n1226-        \"Verify in browser using playwright-skill (in environment with `claude` CLI available): send a simple question 'What is this app?', confirm a response bubble renders within 30s\",\n1227-        \"Typecheck passes\",\n1228-        \"Tests pass\"\n1229-      ],\n1230-      \"priority\": 53,\n1231-      \"passes\": false,\n1232-      \"notes\": \"If Claude Agent SDK does not currently support Max-plan auth without an API key, ship subprocess-only and document the SDK enable path for future. Verify SDK feasibility before committing to dual-path code.\",\n1233-      \"tags\": [\n1234-        \"ui\"\n1235-      ]\n1236-    },\n1237-    {\n1238-      \"id\": \"US-054\",\n1239-      \"title\": \"LessonChat — context builder (active section + lesson metadata → prompt assembly)\",\n1240-      \"description\": \"As the LessonChat backend, I want to build a focused prompt context from the active lesson section + lesson metadata (not the whole lesson), so prompts stay small and responses stay relevant.\",\n1241-      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n1242-        \"src/lib/lessonChat/context.ts exports buildPromptContext({ lesson, currentSectionId? }) → { systemPrompt: string, contextBlock: string }\",\n1243-        \"systemPrompt template: 'You are an AI tutor for an interactive online course. Answer concisely (≤200 words unless code is needed). Stay focused on the lesson topic. If asked off-topic, redirect politely.'\",\n1244-        \"contextBlock includes: lesson.title, lesson.eyebrow, lesson.description, lesson.estimatedMinutes; if currentSectionId given, append the active section's data serialized as text (theory.markdown for theory; question + options for quiz; taskMarkdown for code; etc.)\",\n1245-        \"If currentSectionId not given, append a brief outline: titles of all sections in lesson with their type\",\n1246-        \"Context capped at ~4000 chars total; if exceeded, truncate active section text first and append '… [truncated]'\",\n1247-        \"POST /api/lesson-chat (US-053) wired through buildPromptContext: call with { lesson: <fetched from disk>, currentSectionId: req.body.sectionId }; pass result to connector as { systemPrompt, userMessage: '<contextBlock>\\\\n\\\\nUser question: <message>' }\",\n1248:        \"LessonChat panel (US-052) tracks current scroll position → maps to nearest section heading via IntersectionObserver → sends sectionId in POST body\",\n1249-        \"Vitest tests cover: context built with theory section, with quiz section, without section; truncation when content exceeds 4000 chars\",\n1250-        \"Verify in browser using playwright-skill: scroll to a quiz section in seed lesson, ask 'What is this question testing?', confirm response references the quiz topic specifically (not generic lesson summary)\",\n1251-        \"Typecheck passes\",\n1252-        \"Tests pass\"\n1253-      ],\n1254-      \"priority\": 54,\n1255-      \"passes\": false,\n1256:      \"notes\": \"depends on US-052 + US-053\",\n1257-      \"tags\": [\n1258-        \"ui\"\n1259-      ]\n1260-    },\n1261-    {\n1262-      \"id\": \"US-055\",\n1263-      \"title\": \"LessonChat — streaming responses + Stop/cancel button\",\n1264-      \"description\": \"As a user reading AI tutor responses, I want to see them stream token-by-token and have a Stop button to cancel mid-response, so long answers feel responsive and I can abort if the answer is going off-track.\",\n1265-      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n1266-        \"POST /api/lesson-chat extended to support `Accept: text/event-stream` and respond with SSE stream of assistant tokens (one event per token chunk, with final 'done' event)\",\n1267-        \"Agent SDK connector: use streaming API; subprocess connector: read stdout line-by-line and forward each line as SSE event; close stream on subprocess exit\",\n1268:        \"LessonChat panel (US-052) calls SSE endpoint via EventSource for new messages; appends streamed tokens to assistant bubble in real time\",\n1269:        \"Stop button (placeholder from US-052) becomes active during streaming; click → aborts EventSource on client AND sends DELETE /api/lesson-chat/<requestId> server-side which kills the subprocess / aborts SDK stream\",\n1270-        \"On stop: assistant bubble keeps the partial text + appends italic '— stopped by user' suffix on its own line in --text-tertiary\",\n1271-        \"Server tracks in-flight requests in a Map<requestId, AbortController | childProcess> so DELETE can resolve which to terminate\",\n1272-        \"Auto-cleanup of finished requests from Map after stream end (avoid memory leak)\",\n1273-        \"requestId generated server-side and returned in the first SSE event so client knows what to DELETE\",\n1274-        \"Verify in browser using playwright-skill: send a question that requires a long answer, observe tokens streaming into the assistant bubble, click Stop mid-response, confirm bubble shows partial text + 'stopped by user' suffix, then send a new question and confirm it works\",\n1275-        \"Typecheck passes\",\n1276-        \"Tests pass\"\n1277-      ],\n1278-      \"priority\": 55,\n1279-      \"passes\": false,\n1280-      \"notes\": \"depends on US-053\",\n1281-      \"tags\": [\n1282-        \"ui\"\n1283-      ]\n1284-    },\n1285-    {\n1286-      \"id\": \"US-056\",\n1287-      \"title\": \"Author end-to-end QA test plan markdown (test-plan.md)\",\n1288-      \"description\": \"As a maintainer of this app, I want a single markdown file describing how to manually verify all features end-to-end, including which test courses to generate and which user flows to walk through, so I can sanity-check a release in under an hour.\",\n1289-      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n1290-        \"File written: test-plan.md at repo root\",\n1291-        \"Document structure: Setup section (npm install, npm run dev, etc.) → 'Test Courses to Generate' (≥3 distinct topics chosen to exercise different widget mixes, e.g. one Short narrow topic, one Standard ML topic, one Comprehensive math/CV topic) → 'Walkthroughs' (numbered checklists per area)\",\n1292-        \"Each test course entry includes: topic prompt to enter in Stage 1, refinement choices for Stage 2 (level + duration + theory/practice slider), expected approximate lesson count + module count, which widgets the course is expected to exercise\",\n1293-[Omitted long context line]\n1294-        \"Each walkthrough item is a checkbox with explicit pass criterion (e.g. 'button morphs to Submitted ✓', 'card badge shows In progress · 1/N', 'PNG appears within 10s after first matplotlib install') — no vague 'works correctly'\",\n1295-        \"Document references the relevant US-NNN for each section so failures can be traced back to the originating story\",\n1296-        \"Document includes 'Known limitations' section listing things explicitly out of MVP (multi-user, IndexedDB, tutor without Claude CLI installed, etc.)\",\n1297-        \"Document targets ≤30 minutes for an experienced reviewer to walk through, ≤60 for a new reviewer\",\n1298-        \"Typecheck passes\"\n1299-      ],"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b74a772c-12b8-46f0-a2a8-706cfe2f6baf","uuid":"71ec4bb9-5fdc-4734-b9c0-33ea08d367f3","timestamp":"2026-05-04T05:48:28.230Z","tool_use_result":{"mode":"content","numFiles":0,"filenames":[],"content":"1190:      \"id\": \"US-052\",\n1191-      \"title\": \"LessonChat — sliding side panel UI scaffold + persisted draft in localStorage\",\n1192-      \"description\": \"As a learner, I want a sliding side panel inside lessons where I can compose questions to an AI tutor and have my draft preserved across page reloads, so I can come back to a question without retyping.\",\n1193-      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n1194-        \"Right column of lesson view (US-015 chatCol) becomes a controlled panel: 0px when closed, 320px when open; transition 180ms; prefers-reduced-motion disables animation\",\n1195-        \"Toggle: existing tutor button (⌘.) in lesson toolbar (currently disabled/grey from US-015) becomes active and toggles the panel; ⌘. keyboard shortcut (US-021) likewise toggles\",\n1196-        \"Panel chrome: header with 'AI Tutor' title + close X button; scrollable body for message list; sticky footer with composer (textarea + Send button + Stop button placeholder)\",\n1197-        \"Composer textarea autoresizes (max 6 lines); Enter inserts newline; ⌘+Enter (or Ctrl+Enter) triggers Send; Send button disabled when textarea empty or whitespace-only\",\n1198-        \"Message list area shows placeholder copy when empty: 'Ask anything about this lesson — I have its content as context.' centered, --text-tertiary --fs-sm\",\n1199-        \"Send (in this story) appends a user-message bubble to the message list and clears the textarea — no backend call yet (backend lands in US-053); a placeholder assistant bubble with 'Backend not connected — try again after US-053 ships' is appended for visibility during dev\",\n1200-        \"Draft persistence: textarea value mirrored to `localStorage['lessonChatDraft:<courseSlug>:<lessonSlug>']` on each keystroke (debounced 200ms); restored on mount\",\n1201-        \"Draft cleared from localStorage when message Send appends to message list (text now lives in chat history)\",\n1202-        \"Panel state (open/closed) persisted to `localStorage['lessonChat-open']` (boolean string)\",\n1203-        \"Verify in browser using playwright-skill: ope